{"type":"message","id":"8990ee09","parentId":"d8d67566","timestamp":"2026-03-18T15:35:05.365Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Preparing summary and media**\n\nI see that I need to respond with a summary and include an image as well, possibly appended as MEDIA:url. It's important to emphasize that this is a preliminary summary and not a diagnosis. I want to make sure that the user understands the distinction clearly. So, I'll prepare the summary now and ensure the media is effectively attached. That should give the user a complete and informative response!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_02446c026582dd9e0169bac620ef808191b9158653623b4fd8\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpusYjYUjeMABfDdGAoPQa19p5k6wnMJiMAjkdDxmHnNNaNNkh20XRTmMgH7zbjY9Pi6p_ku6etKgSD8E1H_l26PLmsCH7dg21kzIy9YZXkebJ1WT7RXGPInKkgQje-I9O69p7kWtKtJNDpvz-b9--WOM-JDnj_k9_CPPq88SI25pyRsXXijdzURtILXRZblEpJrYdhivgsfPOl-9HAPda-tQBtoMB_iqb300N78kTmr3I-tKUh9o48fFwOmb6VnxBStkebuzoCpAJmV0QTzbIJl7sSrU2i0KCCnbjx8HmDgJS4WRCN3sI1hrG1EpTMY87v0-Ljvdxeuq6YF1tuQxPouwxckBfVc-8C4m_kGqU5UH2t5-u00an3V6EwuRw5wiw52_b2ZxExxM6oPHil0XeZhGRY54rxFu_k1_hlCjP7EukfDlWR12EclthksuwmJs2IpyBqD5fr_8ZioYMxGkFBCl4bUWFzD2Dd1eauzWPqOmEpNqj0EADvxo_6n_L_a5M7tWG-9olREb0wa97tyFTwTQSp_hBx0KuBxWDrftaOSZX-vxU4-80D2mVMOqSYx5jTI7yX9bnvm77GdSll6vxW_LIQsU1hcUsQcN_mLLQXGXBf3MUwnDLVD8dgYMLlWpNr1lYdOXXM1gQTkWiveG6SgbkYK2dyKDAwuSG5XuEiNyvJrDCHKvujxqrit1PFv6Cd91qP2pz5wN7JywP6m8rubtMuIaAr11b9OSPy-M3nt8gcf8ql2Sb5NQQevO5ERO8xJeBRtUhLLyvUUg-Qg8weGtBkBMEywNtZ8cwIMZ0cRT6iPIRkjzC_C4ohecz28O5vbIJ_9lOVh0GzRKThdbCgR0MGX4vov4PXkw0emzPAj_kKRkuLBnL_HhR-tPDpsPFSYOZ5-iMQFJdzrnaddLHiCyeiBdDNHMig_UiW0EQaE-cAEmcmBixqlrqcPRYAax0-12v\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Preparing summary and media**\\n\\nI see that I need to respond with a summary and include an image as well, possibly appended as MEDIA:url. It's important to emphasize that this is a preliminary summary and not a diagnosis. I want to make sure that the user understands the distinction clearly. So, I'll prepare the summary now and ensure the media is effectively attached. That should give the user a complete and informative response!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] I ran the kidney cancer detection pipeline on your CT image.\n\n**Kidney Cancer Detector module**\n- Kidney detector inference time: **3.27 s**\n- Kidney cancer class: **kidney_tumor**\n- Confidence: **99.9979%**\n\n**Image Analyzer module**\n- Image Analyzer prediction: **kidney_tumor**\n- CAM coverage: **0.0128**\n- CAM center ratio: **0.8250**\n- CAM left-right asymmetry: **0.1000**\n- CAM top-bottom asymmetry: **1.0000**\n- CAM explanation: the model focused on a **small, localized central renal region** with asymmetric spatial distribution, which it interpreted as visually distinct tissue possibly consistent with a localized structural alteration.\n\n**X-AI module**\n- Confidence interpretation: **very high model confidence**, but this is **not a definitive diagnosis**\n- Summary: the pipeline suggests a **high likelihood of kidney cancer** based on the detected renal tumor pattern\n- Visual evidence: the image analysis reported a **kidney tumor signal**\n- Recommended next steps:\n  1. Further medical evaluation with imaging/labs\n  2. Discuss the result with a medical professional\n  3. Consider confirmatory testing such as biopsy or other diagnostic workup\n\n**References**\n- American Cancer Society, *Kidney Cancer: Diagnosis and Treatment* (2022)\n- European Association of Urology, *Imaging in Kidney Cancer* (2020)\n\nImportant: this pipeline output is a **preliminary signal only**, not an actual diagnosis. A radiologist/urologist should confirm any finding with proper clinical review.\n\nMEDIA:http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/admin/retrieve-image-file/nodes_bucket/626130f7c71f6b9e651c76be/69b862e0a6fbd73a6254e5be/b0f1c107-0576-49f4-985a-1754b3411728.jpeg","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_02446c026582dd9e0169bac623c1308191911a7a89171dce95\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":10303,"output":444,"cacheRead":11776,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22523,"cost":{"input":0.025757500000000003,"output":0.00666,"cacheRead":0.002944,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.035361500000000004}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773848092589}}
{"type":"message","id":"fb2ea7ce","parentId":"8990ee09","timestamp":"2026-03-18T15:48:56.949Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"259\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"495506013\",\n  \"sender\": \"Matteo Cicalese\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Wed 2026-03-18 15:48 UTC\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"Matteo Cicalese (495506013)\",\n  \"id\": \"495506013\",\n  \"name\": \"Matteo Cicalese\",\n  \"username\": \"CicaMatt\"\n}\n```\n\nwhat i think is that the skill.md is fucked up, so i'll tell you right away how i want the kidney-pipeline-execution skill to work.\n• the user request to analyze a CT scan of their kidney \n• you upload the image given by the user through that upload endpoint and get the upload path\n• you use that path replacing the placeholder in the json request format in the references folder\n• you send the request to the kidney pipeline endpoint and do the rest as you are doing\n\nthere is an issue with the upload of the image, so make sure to not use placeholder path or things like that.\n\nreview the skill.md and the script implementation, do not fuck up anything, and make sure the revisioned SKILL.md is clearer"}],"timestamp":1773848936946}}
