{"type":"message","id":"f7c37863","parentId":"67052ba0","timestamp":"2026-03-18T15:50:24.372Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_02446c026582dd9e0169bac9a80dd881918904f57ba5bd1c73\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpusmo9c0xzBcNGOI1gYtDy0IodI9r5KLPqeeCVXwQbK6qPrAED3v15Z8g9T8nZZN_Gc6qxiRXUFEwQGZAp5O04BMQ5WzGb70cwTPEoPse2VoMPLkcVQ-fRw4q766JL3Z5i3MRo_hakwR6-WUIgoMMh3p_D8LdB_xG4wXQn8FCeMjghKLDWgmxkr9ReOETDcAWWQ8vJZl3DGOlFB4HFpVjTEO3_BF5uwcnrNuwTEUYxchFrSdoDKn_rCO7KUgfp3-veJPY3pb-qAXuIIbEX3VnOzQlNdKfqB-9pv6ymFYRsaxTy6tY_11v1d9rm44uLXqT-mpTPPV-Imd9u1Yxa2q8Gl6OqPSTOcxqz6LKipSm-9PsI_UCy4dDmnKzHOzXEohaXkcAzQniuagce71_S55AKRg72eSWxBldv9C1PgSDFJjL6jwXYgsuMD4FfSWo087OEZoVuGNMmUydehE3FP76MmLWAwlKBqxwi6kHqI78fcVFoSWMlCg0xMQVTljvFiAbGP2PWR6Fj7Ui8wWWLlPNaOG2O4lBk5a7m1WAJvvuu0MY_IC0j08jMPbn-s_RqcVyMa6L-zJ6I3VYkwGTPq3SpaY4SpsShEeGCpKnlLxUxeNPbwTNHAYXfIGdf_IQyQyax-0htpsdn7KMyp46tIFaRAK6iAlA6G3Zi1x7ZCO3JFI5Wwvzr5Ps8V0pJxd-o9KX53-Rl3UFkZEZxCB6Bw7B_G28fxLp8_YVuFHLhAB5LowQ9MHRg4Sb6QSS_QzTrI0cXdXK6aMViGYJ1ryu7eTcEHWPihucXY05YZssmr1wiqdbnUdXs6FdMC6WjJ6C_yTO0aGFsYKOe8skaOtQaHkvJlEfZX2txIu2cVGQQW_Bv3GNK4k=\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_q3DElvA5iNG9lSPNeKDVQ2Cu|fc_02446c026582dd9e0169bac9a899a481918b19c58283147205","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"~/.openclaw/skills/kidney-pipeline-execution/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: kidney-pipeline-execution\ndescription: Execute the kidney cancer CT pipeline by uploading a user-provided kidney CT image, taking the real uploaded image path returned by the upload endpoint, replacing the image-path placeholder inside the fixed prototype request JSON, then sending that request to the kidney pipeline execution endpoint and summarizing the Kidney Cancer Detector, Image Analyzer, and X-AI outputs. Use when a user wants to run the integrated kidney pipeline on a CT scan image and inspect either the raw response or a clean summary of the main outputs.\n---\n\n# Kidney Pipeline Execution\n\nUpload the user image first, use the returned upload path in the fixed request template, then execute the kidney pipeline.\n\n## Required behavior\n\nFollow this sequence exactly:\n\n1. Determine the local CT image to analyze.\n   - Prefer the explicit user-provided local image path.\n   - If no path is provided, use the newest supported image under `/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound`.\n2. Require the Telegram user id.\n   - Pass it as `--telegram-user-id` or set `TELEGRAM_USER_ID`.\n   - Use that value as the upload request's `user_id` query parameter.\n3. Upload the image with `POST multipart/form-data` to:\n   - `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload?storage_ref=nodes_bucket&local_file_path=upload%2F&user_id=<telegram-user-id>`\n4. Read the upload response JSON.\n   - Build the real remote image path as `path + filename`.\n   - Use the returned path from the upload response only.\n   - Do not keep example paths, stale upload paths, or unresolved placeholders in the executed request.\n5. Load `references/request-template.json`.\n6. Replace every image-path placeholder in the template with the real uploaded image path.\n7. Send the resulting JSON payload to:\n   - `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/prototype_execution/prototype_execution/`\n8. Read the pipeline response and summarize it by module:\n   - Kidney Cancer Detector\n   - Image Analyzer\n   - X-AI\n9. If the analyzer image URL exists at `response.workflows[0].branches[0].nodes[0].children[0].children[0].tracking.parameters.file_path`, extract the URL and include the image in the normal reply.\n10. Do not send out-of-band Telegram messages from the script.\n\n## Fixed values\n\nKeep these values fixed:\n- `storage_ref`: `nodes_bucket`\n- `local_file_path`: `upload/`\n- execution endpoint: `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/prototype_execution/prototype_execution/`\n- request template: `references/request-template.json`\n\n## Implementation notes\n\n- Treat the request template as a fixed prototype payload, but always inject the freshly uploaded image path before execution.\n- Fail loudly if `<image_path_here>` remains anywhere in the payload after replacement.\n- If template fields such as `filename`, `pdf_path`, or `File Path` contain placeholder or stale upload-path values, replace them with the fresh uploaded image path before execution.\n- Preserve the response wrapper shape returned by the script.\n- If the endpoint returns non-JSON text, return that text as the `response` value.\n\n## Preferred script\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/pipeline_execution_tool.py --telegram-user-id <telegram-user-id> [local-image-path]\n```\n\nIf `local-image-path` is omitted, the script should select the newest supported image from `/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound`.\n\n## Summary fields to prioritize\n\nWhen present, summarize these fields first.\n\n### Kidney Cancer Detector\n- `Inference time`\n- `classes`\n- `confidence`\n\n### Image Analyzer\n- `cam_metrics`\n- `prediction`\n- `cam_explanation`\n- `file_path` when useful for returning the analyzer image\n\nWhen `cam_metrics` is present, include all available subfields such as:\n- `coverage`\n- `center_ratio`\n- `lr_asym`\n- `tb_asym`\n\n### X-AI\n- `confidence_interpretation`\n- `recommended_next_steps`\n- `references`\n- `summary`\n- `visual_evidence`\n\nPreserve list order for `recommended_next_steps`.\nPreserve available fields in each reference item such as `title`, `author`, `year`, and `url`.\n\n## User-facing reply rules\n\n- Group the result into the three modules.\n- Use readable labels instead of raw JSON paths.\n- Do not include low-level execution metadata by default.\n- Mention clearly that the pipeline output is a preliminary signal, not a diagnosis.\n- Append the analyzer image itself when an analyzer image URL is available.\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"~/.openclaw/skills/kidney-pipeline-execution/SKILL.md\",\"content\":\"---\\nname: kidney-pipeline-execution\\ndescription: Execute the kidney cancer CT pipeline by uploading a user-provided kidney CT image, taking the real uploaded image path returned by the upload endpoint, replacing the image-path placeholder inside the fixed prototype request JSON, then sending that request to the kidney pipeline execution endpoint and summarizing the Kidney Cancer Detector, Image Analyzer, and X-AI outputs. Use when a user wants to run the integrated kidney pipeline on a CT scan image and inspect either the raw response or a clean summary of the main outputs.\\n---\\n\\n# Kidney Pipeline Execution\\n\\nUpload the user image first, use the returned upload path in the fixed request template, then execute the kidney pipeline.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\nFollow this sequence exactly:\\n\\n1. Determine the local CT image to analyze.\\n   - Prefer the explicit user-provided local image path.\\n   - If no path is provided, use the newest supported image under `/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound`.\\n2. Require the Telegram user id.\\n   - Pass it as `--telegram-user-id` or set `TELEGRAM_USER_ID`.\\n   - Use that value as the upload request's `user_id` query parameter.\\n3. Upload the image with `POST multipart/form-data` to:\\n   - `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload?storage_ref=nodes_bucket&local_file_path=upload%2F&user_id=<telegram-user-id>`\\n4. Read the upload response JSON.\\n   - Build the real remote image path as `path + filename`.\\n   - Use the returned path from the upload response only.\\n   - Do not keep example paths, stale upload paths, or unresolved placeholders in the executed request.\\n5. Load `references/request-template.json`.\\n6. Replace every image-path placeholder in the template with the real uploaded image path.\\n7. Send the resulting JSON payload to:\\n   - `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/prototype_execution/prototype_execution/`\\n8. Read the pipeline response and summarize it by module:\\n   - Kidney Cancer Detector\\n   - Image Analyzer\\n   - X-AI\\n9. If the analyzer image URL exists at `response.workflows[0].branches[0].nodes[0].children[0].children[0].tracking.parameters.file_path`, extract the URL and include the image in the normal reply.\\n10. Do not send out-of-band Telegram messages from the script.\\n\\n## Fixed values\\n\\nKeep these values fixed:\\n- `storage_ref`: `nodes_bucket`\\n- `local_file_path`: `upload/`\\n- execution endpoint: `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/prototype_execution/prototype_execution/`\\n- request template: `references/request-template.json`\\n\\n## Implementation notes\\n\\n- Treat the request template as a fixed prototype payload, but always inject the freshly uploaded image path before execution.\\n- Fail loudly if `<image_path_here>` remains anywhere in the payload after replacement.\\n- If template fields such as `filename`, `pdf_path`, or `File Path` contain placeholder or stale upload-path values, replace them with the fresh uploaded image path before execution.\\n- Preserve the response wrapper shape returned by the script.\\n- If the endpoint returns non-JSON text, return that text as the `response` value.\\n\\n## Preferred script\\n\\nRun:\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 scripts/pipeline_execution_tool.py --telegram-user-id <telegram-user-id> [local-image-path]\\n```\\n\\nIf `local-image-path` is omitted, the script should select the newest supported image from `/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound`.\\n\\n## Summary fields to prioritize\\n\\nWhen present, summarize these fields first.\\n\\n### Kidney Cancer Detector\\n- `Inference time`\\n- `classes`\\n- `confidence`\\n\\n### Image Analyzer\\n- `cam_metrics`\\n- `prediction`\\n- `cam_explanation`\\n- `file_path` when useful for returning the analyzer image\\n\\nWhen `cam_metrics` is present, include all available subfields such as:\\n- `coverage`\\n- `center_ratio`\\n- `lr_asym`\\n- `tb_asym`\\n\\n### X-AI\\n- `confidence_interpretation`\\n- `recommended_next_steps`\\n- `references`\\n- `summary`\\n- `visual_evidence`\\n\\nPreserve list order for `recommended_next_steps`.\\nPreserve available fields in each reference item such as `title`, `author`, `year`, and `url`.\\n\\n## User-facing reply rules\\n\\n- Group the result into the three modules.\\n- Use readable labels instead of raw JSON paths.\\n- Do not include low-level execution metadata by default.\\n- Mention clearly that the pipeline output is a preliminary signal, not a diagnosis.\\n- Append the analyzer image itself when an analyzer image URL is available.\\n\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":159,"output":1111,"cacheRead":39808,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":41078,"cost":{"input":0.0003975,"output":0.016665,"cacheRead":0.009951999999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.027014499999999997}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773848998650}}
