h_here>` survives** in the payload before execution\n- **request-template.json** was cleaned so stale embedded paths were changed to placeholders where relevant\n\nVerification:\n- I ran the revised script end-to-end.\n- It executed successfully.\n- The payload used the **fresh uploaded path**, not the old hardcoded sample path.\n- I confirmed the returned request echo now shows the fresh uploaded path in:\n  - `filename`\n  - `pdf_path`\n  - `File Path`\n\nWhat it means:\n- The skill now matches exactly the behavior you described.\n- The main upload-path bug class is covered: the pipeline request should no longer accidentally carry stale template image paths.\n\nNext sensible step:\n- If you want, I can do one more cleanup pass on `request-template.json` to remove other noisy tracking/example fields that are not needed for execution, but I left that alone for now to avoid breaking the working payload.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_02446c026582dd9e0169bac9ccdf888191b73a8f1ac817a03c\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":10288,"output":370,"cacheRead":41088,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":51746,"cost":{"input":0.025720000000000003,"output":0.00555,"cacheRead":0.010272,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.04154200000000001}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773849035258}}
