ach time\n- but the analyzer output and final image stay exactly the same\n- that usually means either:\n  - the upload API is returning a path without really storing the new file correctly, or\n  - the pipeline backend is resolving to old data despite the new path\n\nSo yes: your observation is consistent with the evidence.\n\nBest next step:\n- I should add a **post-upload verification step** in the script:\n  - after upload, try to confirm the uploaded file is actually retrievable or usable\n  - only then call the pipeline\n  - otherwise fail early with a clear “upload did not really stick” error\n\nIf you want, I can implement that now in the skill script, carefully.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_02446c026582dd9e0169bacb9d13a88191aa4eba3e5033317e\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":215,"output":312,"cacheRead":72960,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":73487,"cost":{"input":0.0005375,"output":0.00468,"cacheRead":0.01824,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0234575}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773849497033}}
